pub(super) const AFTER_HITTING: &str = "Hitting is the one thing here that is not a row to repair around: say plainly, and today, that it will not happen again. Then the repair - sorry without a but after it, name what happened, and say what you will do instead. Then make the moment less likely, because most of this comes from the ten minutes when everyone wants something at once: pick the two flashpoints, getting out of the door and bedtime, and change the routine rather than your patience - shoes by the door the night before, a five-minute warning before bed. When you feel it rising, put your hands behind your back, breathe out for longer than you breathe in, and say \"I need a minute\" and leave the room. A parent who steps out for a minute is doing better than one who stays and escalates. If it has happened more than once, or you are frightened of what you might do, say it out loud to someone today - your health visitor, 111, or a parenting line - because that is the step that keeps it from happening again.";
pub(super) const AFTER_SHOUTING: &str = "The repair matters more than the resolve: say sorry plainly, name what happened - \"I shouted about the shoes\" - and say what you will do instead. Then make the moment less likely, because most of this comes from the ten minutes when everyone wants something at once: pick the two flashpoints, getting out of the door and bedtime, and change the routine rather than your patience - shoes by the door the night before, a five-minute warning before bed. When you feel it rising, put your hands behind your back, breathe out for longer than you breathe in, and say \"I need a minute\" and leave the room. A parent who steps out for a minute is doing better than one who stays and escalates.";
